# Match rules

Follow the project skill `.agents/skills/add-match-rule/SKILL.md`. Design notes: `docs/deployment-plan/spike-11/comparison-layers.md`, `docs/matching-model.md`.

- Layer packages are pure: no `core/database`, no build tags; non-test files import no `core/matchregistry`, and only `core/subjectprofile` imports `core/autoreconcile`, to turn its output into a profile.
- Numbers live only in `core/matchregistry`; a layer holds no numeric literal other than 0 and 1.
- A new knob is a `Rules` field, a registry value with its source, and a row in the knob inventory.
- A new comparer needs a sample row and a generator in `contract_test.go`.
- Check: the commands in the skill's Check section.
